(a) No individual or group or association of individuals, shall either;
(1) Operate a gun club as defined in section 10-40 in Elbert County; or
(2) Advertise a location in Elbert County as a gun club; or
(3) Sell or provide ammunition at the site of a firing range in Elbert County: without first obtaining a conditional use permit upon compliance with the requirements of chapter 11.02 of the Elbert County Zoning Ordinance.
(b) Every application for conditional use permit shall contain, in addition to the items required by chapter 11.02 of the Elbert County Zoning Ordinance, the following:
(1) Name of the gun club;
(2) The name, address, telephone number, and email address of the individual or individuals responsible for the gun club;
(3) A site plan drawn to scale showing the location of all buildings, signage, parking area, fencing, targets, firing lines, ready lines, backstops, and berms, and showing the distance from each to the nearest property line or road;
(4) An accurate sketch showing the slope of ground level from the firing lines to the backstops and from the firing lines to the berms;
(5) The proposed days and hours of operation;
(6) A copy of the proposed safety plan, which shall address permissible firearms, general range rules, gun handling rules, and shall provide for the presence of an identified range safety officer on site at all times of operation;
(7) A copy of a final report of a NRA Range Technical Team Evaluation, which shall include the expected decibel level the proposed operation will create and the standard of noise reduction possible, and which shall conclude that the operation as proposed meets all applicable standards established by the NRA Range Source Book published the National Rifle Association; and
(8) A notarized statement from the individual or individuals responsible for the gun club acknowledging that the permit may be revoked or suspended if the operation fails to meet all applicable standards established by the NRA Range Source Book published the National Rifle Association.
(Code 1996, § 46-21; Ord. of 4-9-2001(3), § 2; Ord. of 02-10-2025(1), § 4)

