It shall be unlawful for any person to establish, operate or maintain any junkyard, any portion of which is within 1,000 feet of the nearest edge of the right-of-way of any state highway or county road, except a junkyard that is:
(1) Screened by natural objects, plantings, fences or other appropriate means, or which is otherwise removed from sight so as not to be visible from the main traveled way of such highway systems;
(2) Located within areas which are zoned for industrial use under authority of law;
(3) Located within unzoned industrial areas, which areas shall be determined from actual land uses and defined by requirements promulgated by the board of commissioners; and
(4) Not visible from the main traveled way of the systems.
(Code 1996, § 34-47; Ord. of 9-13-1993, § 2)
